            <ArticleTitle>Ovarian cancer and the immune system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-58</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.gore.2017.01.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Short communication in response to the review of Turner et al. entitled &quot;Ovarian cancer and the immune system - the role of targeted therapies&quot; published in Gynecological Oncology. We believe systemic immune parameters might be a good alternative to tumor biopsy to gain insight in the immunological background of ovarian cancer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
